{"seq":15,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T09:29:43.328Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"6bf845defd17596040e2c4fb29b538c65908c75af2460a6b84f8169fda19d2e2","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes I can see (the team digests under teams/team-north and teams/team-central). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers came up:\n\n- #PD-4492: in \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't sending SMS bay assignments for Dock Doors 14-18. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n- #4419: in \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell when that happened.\n\nThings I left out:\n- Moss's 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and 2026-03-23 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Central accounts (Marrow), not QFL.\n- Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" intel note is about a different company. It isn't a Pemberline customer.\n\nI only checked Moss's notes, not the QFL incident channel or other sources."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
